BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232803Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment. The interdisciplinary\, open and collaborative platform fosters 
 creative exchange among artists\, scientists\, writers and other professio
 nals\, with residents initiating participatory local activities that conne
 ct them with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activities\,
  sharing sessions\, media promotion and exhibition opportunities. CYCLES: 
 Spring 2028 (April to June) and Autumn 2028 (July to October)\, each appro
 ximately eight weeks. WHAT YOU GET (International Residency Fellowship\, f
 ully funded): private studio and accommodation\, round-trip economy airfar
 e or second-class train within a set budget\, a production grant of RMB 10
 \,000 per person or team for materials and production (excluding living ex
 penses)\, community engagement and cultural experiences\, media promotion 
 and networking. ELIGIBILITY: multidisciplinary creators worldwide\, includ
 ing visual and performing artists\, musicians\, filmmakers\, architects\, 
 curators\, designers and creatives with interdisciplinary backgrounds brid
 ging art\, business and culture. APPLICATION: free\; submit a photo\, port
 folio\, CV and project proposal in English and Chinese to a4residency@a4am
 .cn\, with the subject line specifying the programme tier and preferred cy
 cle. DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 for the 2028 full-year recruitment. A para
 llel self-funded light track exists\; this listing covers the funded fello
 wship only.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLoca
 tion: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwi
 de.\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, ro
 und-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\
 , and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and 
 production (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: App
 roximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (Ju
 ly to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residency
 artcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:design-trust-seed-feature-impact-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261024T232803Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Deadline: Design Trust Seed\, Feature & Impact Grants (Hong Kong / 
 Greater Bay Area)
DESCRIPTION:Design Trust offers grants to individual designers\, curators\,
  collectives\, and non-profit organisations for projects and activities re
 levant to various design disciplines\, supporting work relevant to the con
 text and content of Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area (the Special Admini
 strative Regions of Hong Kong and Macao and the nine Guangdong municipalit
 ies of Guangzhou\, Shenzhen\, Zhuhai\, Foshan\, Huizhou\, Dongguan\, Zhong
 shan\, Jiangmen\, and Zhaoqing). It supports innovative\, thought-provokin
 g investigations across design disciplines from graphics\, media\, and wea
 rables to architecture and the built environment\, including exhibitions\,
  research projects\, and creative installations that advocate the positive
  role of design in the region. THREE GRANTS: (1) SEED GRANT (HKD 50\,000) 
 fosters experimentation\, testing\, and sharing\, awarded to individuals k
 ick-starting a meaningful project with social\, educational\, economical\,
  or environmental impact\; supports emerging designers\, young scholars\, 
 and projects in the pipeline needing additional resources\, including rese
 arch and prototypes focused on Hong Kong and Greater Bay Area issues to be
  showcased at international venues\, symposia\, or biennales. (2) FEATURE 
 GRANT (capped at HKD 300\,000\, awarded annually upon special consideratio
 n) fosters cross-disciplinary projects on the Greater Bay Area with wide-r
 eaching audiences\, often sited at an exhibition or biennale of internatio
 nal standing\, supporting exchange between a Hong Kong/China-based collect
 ive and an internationally renowned cultural institution. (3) IMPACT GRANT
  supports public-facing\, community-based projects led by former Design Tr
 ust grant recipients\, fellows\, and mentees with a proven track record\; 
 considered case-by-case (contact grantapplication@designtrust.hk). ELIGIBI
 LITY: individuals\, collectives\, and certified non-profit organisations e
 ither based in the Greater Bay Area or seeking support for design projects
  related to the region. Individuals or collectives who have completed two 
 Feature Grants or three Seed Grants should apply for the Impact Grant inst
 ead. APPLICATION: two cycles annually\, deadlines 20 April and 20 October 
 (late submissions roll to the next cycle)\; apply at least 3 to 6 months b
 efore the project's commencement. Design Trust may provide full or partial
  funding on a case-by-case basis.\n\nOrganisation: Design Trust\nLocation:
  Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. Open to applicants based in the regio
 n or seeking support for design projects related to it\, including interna
 tional applicants.\nAward: Seed Grant: HKD 50\,000. Feature Grant: capped 
 at HKD 300\,000\, awarded annually upon special consideration. Impact Gran
 t: case-by-case\, for former grantees. Full or partial funding on a case-b
 y-case basis. Free to apply.\nDuration: Two grant cycles annually (deadlin
 es 20 April and 20 October)\; apply 3 to 6 months before project commencem
 ent\n\nMore: https://designtrust.hk/grants/dtgrants/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://designtrust.hk/grants/dtgrants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. Open to applicants based in th
 e region or seeking support for design projects related to it\, including 
 international applicants.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232803Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:white-rabbit-gallery-wrg-digital-generation-xi-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232803Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: WRG Digital Call-Out: Generation Xi (White Rabbit Gallery
 )
DESCRIPTION:White Rabbit Gallery in Sydney commissions an emerging artist o
 r designer to create a short digital animation responding to its Generatio
 n Xi exhibition\, which looks at China's youth amid the AI\, robotics and 
 EV revolution\, and to the New Ugly digital design aesthetic. The commissi
 oned work (up to 20 seconds\, minimum 1280x720 at 16:9\, max 150MB\, inclu
 ding the exhibition title in English and Mandarin) is displayed for five m
 onths on the gallery's website landing page and enters the permanent WRG D
 igital Archive. SUPPORT: AUD 2\,000 artist fee (split equally if a collabo
 rative group) plus mentorship from creative agency Spring in Alaska during
  the development period (28 September - 2 November 2026). ELIGIBILITY: ope
 n internationally to applicants 18+ within the first 10 years of their art
 istic or design practice who are not represented by a commercial gallery o
 r design agency and not employed by a design company\; students and collec
 tives welcome. Free to enter. Deadline: 14 September 2026\, 5pm AEST.\n\nO
 rganisation: White Rabbit Gallery\nLocation: Online (gallery in Sydney\, A
 ustralia)\; no travel required\nAward: AUD 2\,000 artist fee (split equall
 y if a collaborative group)\; free to enter\nDuration: Development period 
 28 September - 2 November 2026 with mentorship\; commissioned work display
 ed 5 months on the gallery website plus permanent WRG Digital Archive incl
 usion\n\nMore: https://whiterabbitcollection.org/wrg-digital-call-out/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://whiterabbitcollection.org/wrg-digital-call-out/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (gallery in Sydney\, Australia)\; no travel required
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cifnl-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232803Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Industries Fund NL: Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL offers one residency at Videota
 ge\, the Hong Kong media art institute (est. 1986) known for critical work
  on XR\, AI\, blockchain and video games. The 2027 edition takes the techn
 ological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point: deep neural network
 s now shape social media\, healthcare\, finance\, governance and justice w
 hile their inner workings remain hard to grasp\, and the resident is invit
 ed to explore this through media art in Hong Kong's urban context. WHO: an
  individual designer\, maker or observer within digital culture\, establis
 hed in the Netherlands or the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom\, registered 
 with the KvK (or another Kingdom business register)\, with at least four y
 ears of professional practice. NOT for duos\, collectives\, or recipients 
 of CIFNL Talent Development\, Self-taught Designer or Emerging Design Prac
 tices ABCSSS grants during the work period (winning this excludes applying
  to those schemes in 2027). SUPPORT: EUR 5\,000 (two months) or EUR 6\,500
  (three months) for travel\, insurance\, living costs\, time and materials
 \; housing\, workspace\, curatorial guidance and production costs are paid
  directly to Videotage\; accommodation arranged by Videotage\; access to e
 quipment and the Videotage Media Art Collection archive. SELECTION: tender
 -style ranking by an external advisory committee on artistic quality\, pro
 ject quality and motivation\; the top five proposals go to Videotage\, whi
 ch co-decides\; decision within eight weeks of closing. APPLY via the Fund
 's application platform (aanvragen.stimuleringsfonds.nl)\, round 'Open Cal
 l Residencies 2027'\, preferably in English: work plan (max 4 A4 / 4 MB PD
 F)\, brief CV (max 2 A4)\, portfolio (max 8 A4 / 8 MB)\, certified KvK ext
 ract under one year old\, and a representative JPG image. NOTE: account ac
 tivation on the platform takes one working day\, so register early. DEADLI
 NE: 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Industries Fun
 d NL (Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie)\, with Videotage\nLocation: H
 ong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in the Neth
 erlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarte
 n and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business register (KvK)
 .\nAward: One residency grant: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month work period or E
 UR 6\,500 for three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses
 \, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport costs. Hous
 ing\, work space\, Videotage guidance and production costs are paid by the
  Fund directly to Videotage on top of the grant\; accommodation is arrange
 d by Videotage. No application fee.\nDuration: 23 March to 18 May 2027 (tw
 o months) or 23 March to 15 June 2027 (three months)\; state your preferre
 d period. Research period plus a concluding public presentation event for 
 Videotage's Hong Kong network.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/e
 n/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regis
 ter (KvK).
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
